            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Arun1194",
                        "email": "rarun@ami.com",
                        "username": "Arun1194"
                    },
                    "message": "The changes look reasonable for updating to clang-20. \n\nQuick question: Were any of the removed checks causing false \npositives, or were they just not applicable? Asking for context."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I answered this in the commit message, right?\n\n```\n* Remove all undocumented checks[1].\n* Remove all checks not applicable to OpenBMC environment.\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "style/cpp/.clang-tidy",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jayanth Othayoth",
                        "email": "ojayanth@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ojayanth"
                    },
                    "message": "Nit : it will be good add Reference documentaion Link https://releases.llvm.org/21.1.0/tools/clang/tools/extra/docs/clang-tidy/checks/list.html"
                },
                {
                    "file": "style/cpp/.clang-tidy",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Added a reference in an earlier commit in this stack."
                },
                {
                    "file": "style/cpp/.clang-tidy",
                    "line": 111,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jayanth Othayoth",
                        "email": "ojayanth@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ojayanth"
                    },
                    "message": "Checks ending with -c are C-specific CERT rules, Ids this document planing to support c/C++ mixed or Cpp only?\nIt will be good to add note in the  document this scope decision for clarity."
                },
                {
                    "file": "style/cpp/.clang-tidy",
                    "line": 111,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Checks ending in `-c` are _not` C-specific.  They are checks that are at least relevant for C but are quite likely also relevant for C++.  For example, `cert-flp30-c` is just as viable for C++ code as it is for C code."
                },
                {
                    "file": "style/cpp/.clang-tidy",
                    "line": 176,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jayanth Othayoth",
                        "email": "ojayanth@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ojayanth"
                    },
                    "message": "Typo: clang-analyzer-optin.taint.GenericTaint ( analyzer spelling, camel-case GenericTaint)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "style/cpp/.clang-tidy",
                    "line": 176,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "style/cpp/.clang-tidy",
                    "line": 179,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jayanth Othayoth",
                        "email": "ojayanth@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ojayanth"
                    },
                    "message": "cppcoreguidelines-avoid-c-arrays is an alias of modernize-avoid-c-arrays . Remove this and keep the base modernize-avoid-c-arrays"
                },
                {
                    "file": "style/cpp/.clang-tidy",
                    "line": 179,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
